This post has been a long time coming, in several ways:

I've been playing on and off since 3 was released without ascending
(mostly due to lack of patience on my part and not being properly
prepared for Gehennom, or sheer carelessness). My previous best was to
have reached the top of the wizard's tower before being overwhelmed
when someone got carried away summoning friends.

The game was played over the course of about 5 weeks;

I actually ascended over a month ago but haven't posted up until now
because of certain deficiencies in my news setup, so this won't be
very detailed.

Sokoban gave the bag of holding. The mines end (wine cellar) had a
silver dragon, who left scales, later converted. Very handy. I donated
enough to the minetown priest to get 10 points of divine protection.
The main dungeon was no trouble, and I gained several artifact weapons
from sacrificing, choosing to keep Mjollnir and Grayswandir. Forgot I
was a dwarf and sacrificed a bugbear, causing Yeenoghu to
appear. Fortunately he wasn't much bother. Thrones gave 2 genocides
which went on my pet hates, master mind flayers and arch-liches.

The quest was simple, and I emerged with strength somewhere around
18/70 and 15 tins of fire giant meat to top it up.

I carelessly lost Mjollnir in the moat at Fort Ludios when on one
occasion it didn't return, and had to return with an amulet of magical
breathing to go diving for it. The castle was easy enough, anything I
didn't want to fight getting squashed by the drawbridge.

Wishes at the castle went on scrolls of charging, speed boots, cloak
of magis resistance, ring of levitation, magic markers. I can't
remember what the rest were for.

Gehennom wasn't too bad; though I'd made it there many times before I
had never been quite prepared enough. This time I had spent the time
working on my armour class and making holy water. You can never have
too much holy water (except when you have to carry it). I *will* learn
to make stashes in future.

Orcus gated in Baalzebub for backup, but he soon went
down to Grayswandir. Vlad was a pushover as usual.

Getting past the wizard's tower and finding the vibrating aquare was a
first for me, and this was when I began to think I actually had a
chance to ascend and started being a bit more careful. Not too careful
though, as I displaced a pet baluchitherium into the water on
Juiblex's level. I never bothered to mollify Tyr, and forgetting this
later in the game prayed and got no help at all.

Playing late at night I lost divine protection to a gremlin. I went
back up and gave all the gold from Ludios to priests without getting
it back. Not good.

My next near-fatal mistake was being burdened when I woke the
wizard. Won't do that again. Also killed him over the moat and had to
go diving again for the book.

The sanctum didn't seem too hard. I was concerned at what the high
priest might do, but just as I was about to take him on a cockatrice
came along and left a corpse, which made that a non-issue.

Going back up the dungeon, the mysterious force must have kicked in at
least a dozen times. I saw far too much of level 31 in particular.

On to the elemental planes, the Orb showed the way to the portals,
though it took several attempts to find each one and I had to recharge
it. Earth took time to dig through and fight off the elementals; air
was tedious through being repeatedly engulfed by air elementals and
having to recover in vortexes which couldn't harm me. Fire and water
took almost no time.

And so to the astral plane. Going for the right hand altar first, it
was heavy going and Death lowered my max HP by around 50. Wrong
altar. Then another convenient cockatrice appeared and the way to the
centre altar was much easier. Also wrong.

Going for the final altar I was overwhelmed and my HP finally ran
out. One amulet of life saving used. If I had remembered the one in my
bag I would have put it on at this point, but it was late and I'd
forgotten I had a spare. No matter, I was almost there. A few more
whacks and the way was clear, and I offered the amulet.

The voice of Tyr booms: "Congratulations, mortal!"--More--
